# A list of security issues that we have accepted the risk

# update after mainnet fixes
GHSA-82j2-j2ch-gfr8

# yamux 0.12.1 is linked transitively via libp2p-yamux 0.47 (dual 0.12/0.13 backend) but is never
# instantiated: both yamux Config call sites (consensus network constructor + rayls-relay test client)
# use a bare Config::default() with no setters, which selects the 0.13.10 backend
# (Either::Right(Config013)). The 0.12 impl is dead code on our paths and cannot be negotiated by a
# remote peer (both speak the same /yamux/1.0.0 wire protocol; the impl is chosen locally).
# 0.12.1 is also not itself vulnerable to this panic: its inbound-SYN path validates the body
# length BEFORE creating the stream, so the create-then-drop -> `expect("stream not found")`
# path is unreachable. The vulnerable window was the 0.13.0-0.13.9
# rewrite; we run the patched 0.13.10.
# NOTE: any yamux Config setter (set_max_num_streams / set_receive_window_size /
# set_window_update_mode) or Config::client()/::server() would silently switch the backend to 0.12.1.
# The call sites carry a
# "YAMUX BACKEND GUARD" comment -- keep them setter-free.
# Removal is not possible today: we currently pin libp2p 0.56.0 and its libp2p-yamux 0.47 hard-requires
# both backends. Re-check this when libp2p releases a version whose libp2p-yamux drops the 0.12
# backend, or if any code starts using Config::client()/::server()/WindowUpdateMode (the 012 paths).
CVE-2026-32314

# hickory-resolver 0.25.2 is pulled in on two edges: libp2p-dns 0.44 (via libp2p 0.56) and
# reth-dns-discovery (via reth v1.11.0).
# GHSA-5j98-2g5x-46v6 (HIGH): with DNSSEC validation ENABLED, Resolver::lookup()/lookup_ip()
# return Ok() for responses that failed DNSSEC validation (bogus), instead of an error.
# Accepted risk for now:
#   - The vulnerable path is unreachable in our stack. Neither consumer enables DNSSEC
#     validation: both build their resolvers from system configuration with NO trust anchors,
#     so no validation runs and a bogus response can never be returned as validated.
#   - A clean fix needs reth >= v2.3.0 (its hickory-resolver requirement moves to ^0.26.1,
#     which unifies with a 0.26.3 direct dep), which in turn lets us bump libp2p 0.56 -> 0.57
#     (libp2p-dns 0.45 -> hickory ^0.26) to keep the single-copy lockstep invariant.
# Resolution: land the reth v1.11.0 -> v2.3.0+ bump (tracked as a separate task), then bump
# libp2p + the direct hickory-resolver dep to 0.26.x, verify hickory-resolver 0.25.x is gone
# from Cargo.lock, and remove this entry.
GHSA-5j98-2g5x-46v6
